 		<English>[H1]Military Advisor Battles Legend[\H1][PARAGRAPH:2]Battle rows are shown from the inspected player's perspective: "Our" columns always describe the inspected player's unit, "Their" columns describe the opponent. The dropdown selects whose perspective is shown.[PARAGRAPH:2][H2]Columns[\H2][NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Turn / Year: when the battle happened.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Result (emoji): three distinct emojis, one for each outcome — won, lost, or retreat (combat ended without a death).[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Est%: simple strength-share estimate from starting effective strengths: our strength divided by both units' combined strength. It is not exact Civ4 combat odds because first strikes, withdrawal, damage rounds, etc. are not modeled here.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Role (emoji): emoji shown when the inspected player initiated the attack; blank when defending or when role is unknown.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Strength icon b: base XML strength of the unit (no modifiers).[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Strength icon s: starting effective strength at combat begin (with all modifiers applied).[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Strength icon e: ending effective strength after combat damage was applied.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Strength icon m: maximum effective strength (full health, with modifiers).[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]XP: unit experience before combat; yellow XP marks a Great-General-led unit.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Our Unit / Their Unit: the units that fought; click to open Sevopedia entry. Unit name shown in yellow when that unit was led by a Great General.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Civ / Leader icons (Their side only): opponent civ and leader; click to open Sevopedia entry.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]PID: opponent player ID.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Cap#: colored capture count from inspected-player perspective. Green = we captured this many of their units; red = they captured this many of ours; blank = no capture.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Cap (icon): captured unit type when applicable; click to open Sevopedia entry.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Hill/Peak / Terrain / Feature (optional, gated by SAS define): plot context where the combat occurred; click to open Sevopedia entry.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Plot (icon): click to close the advisor and center the camera on the battle plot. Three distinct icons cover open-field battle, defended city (still standing for original owner), and city fell during this battle.[PARAGRAPH:2][H2]Strength Color Coding[\H2][NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Effective strength columns are color-coded relative to the unit's max effective strength: white at full, green above 66%, yellow above 33%, red at 33% or below.[PARAGRAPH:2][H2]Sorting and Logging[\H2][NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Click any column header to sort numerically/alphabetically.[NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]The LOG button (when enabled via SAS define) writes the visible battle history to PythonDbg.log for external inspection.[PARAGRAPH:2][H2]Blank Values[\H2][NEWLINE][ICON_BULLET]Blank cells can mean the value is zero or not applicable (for example, the lost unit died, no worker was captured), or that the row was not recorded fully for some reason (early version of this feature, bug to fix, etc.).</English>
